{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"singleton","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}]},{"text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The determinism requirement","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}]},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other’s, and after sync ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}]},{"text":" rows are gone.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"code":"collapse(collapse(rows))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" must keep the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}]},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","role":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistableModel"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistableModel"}],"title":"PersistableModel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","title":"SwiduxPersistence","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","title":"EntityDB","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","title":"byID(preferring:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapses rows sharing an "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" down to one, keeping the winner of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"choose","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}